# Applies to the root Dockerfile's build context (docker build -t bitcode-hrm:latest .).
# Two things this protects against, independently of the Dockerfile's own COPY list:
#   1. A leaner, faster build context (nothing here is ever needed to build or run the app).
#   2. Defense in depth: if someone ever builds locally (where node_modules/.next/.env
#      genuinely exist on disk, unlike GitHub Actions' fresh checkout), none of it can
#      leak into the image even before the Dockerfile's own COPY list is considered.

# Dependencies — always reinstalled inside the image, never copied in from the host
node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Build output — always rebuilt inside the image
.next
out
.test-build

# Version control
.git
.github

# Env files — must never be baked into an image
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Docs (this repo keeps a lot of design/report markdown at the root and under docs/) —
# useful to humans, not needed to build or run the app
*.md
docs

# Test / lint / coverage artifacts
coverage
playwright-report
eslint-report.json
*.tsbuildinfo
tsconfig.test.json
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx

# Logs, data dumps, editor/OS noise
*.log
*.csv
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea

# The postgres image has its own separate build context (./docker/postgres) — not needed
# to build the app image
docker

# Claude Code project-local scratch, if present
.claude
